\title{Feast of St. Matthew 2026}
\tag{cmc}
\date{2026-09-20}
\author{liamoc}
\quote{
Salus pópuli ego sum, dicit Dóminus: de quacúmque tribulatióne clamáverint ad me, exáudiam eos: et ero illórum Dóminus in perpétuum. \br
Eúntes, docéte omnes gentes, baptizántes eos, et docéntes eos serváre ómnia quæcúmque mandávi vobis, dicit Dóminus.
}

\p{Today I returned to my usual [All Saints Ainslie](https://www.allsaintsainslie.org.au/) in the morning where we sang Mozart's [Ave Verum Corpus](https://youtu.be/7AqGrEnx4C8) under my (metaphorical) baton: }
\quote{
\table{
  \tr{
    \td{
      Ave verum corpus natum de María Vírgine;
    }\td{Hail, true body, born of the Virgin Mary;}
  }\tr{
    \td{Vere passum, immolátum in cruce pro hómine;
      }
    \td{True suffering, sacrificed on the cross for Man;}
  }
  \tr{\td{Cuius latus perforátum unda fluxit et sánguine} \td{From whose pierced side flowed waves of blood,}}
  \tr{
    \td{ 
      Esto nobis prægustátum in mortis examine.}
    \td{Be for us a foretaste in death's trial.}
}}
}
\p{I'm still annoyed by the anticipation of the feast day, but I don't think the rector is movable on this subject.}